5. CONSIDERATION
================================================================================

Royalties are payable to Etienne Cimon. Commercial relationships are
administered through GlobecSys Inc. ("GSys"); the contracting entity and
structure are at the rights holder's discretion and are fixed in the executed
agreement.

Royalty basis is set per agreement and is typically structured on one or more
of: per-unit shipped, per-tape-out or per-mask-set, per-design-win, or an
annual site license. Consideration for the warranty, indemnity and support
elements of sections 3.4 to 3.6 is priced separately from the closed-product
and closed-modification rights of sections 3.1 to 3.2.

Consideration under section 3.7 -- internal production by an AI or datacentre
operator, across the whole tier R corpus -- is priced separately from the
above and is ordinarily NOT per-unit, because no unit is Conveyed. Bases in
ordinary use are: an annual fleet license scaled to deployed accelerator die
or to installed compute capacity; a per-tape-out or per-mask-set fee; a term
site license per design centre; or a combination. Where the operator takes
only some of the elements enumerated in section 3.7 -- most commonly
indemnity and support without closed modifications -- those elements are
priced individually.

Consideration for tier P case 2 material under section 4.5 is independent of
both, because no open path exists for that material and the question of
Conveyance does not arise. It is the only element of this document that is
chargeable for internal production as such, rather than by election of the
Licensee.

